### Approach
1. **Understanding Fixed Permutations**: A permutation remains unchanged after converting its standard cyclic representation back into a permutation if each cycle in the permutation is structured such that the maximum element in the cycle points to the next element in the cycle, and all other elements point to the maximum element. This ensures that when the parentheses are removed, the permutation remains the same.
2. **Generating Valid Permutations**: Valid permutations can be generated by considering all possible ways to partition the set {1, 2, ..., n} into cycles where each cycle starts with its maximum element. The cycles are then ordered by their maximum elements.
